        "gdb/thread.c:880-886",
        "gdb/linux-nat.c:3455-3468"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Exact selected-child scheduling then cannot newly grant original-thread resume under those invariants; scheduling flags alone do not prove exclusion. Native execution can occur before later commit.",
      "refs": [
        "gdb/infrun.c:2387-2424",
        "gdb/infrun.c:3674-3783",
        "gdb/linux-nat.c:1764-1830",
        "gdb/linux-nat.c:3512-3601"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Global inline step-over state can defer the child. This is a conditional safety proof, without unconditional command completion or actual child exit evidence.",
      "refs": [
        "gdb/infrun.c:1490-1496",
        "gdb/infrun.c:2151-2161",
